    "description": "Participating in the SEC Directed Internship was a pivotal experience, offering a unique platform to bridge the gap between academic learning and real-world application. This six-week immersion allowed me to collaborate with a diverse team of four interns, working in tandem to develop and present a proof of concept Python-based AI solution. Our project addressed the critical issue of overdiagnosis of pneumonia in children, achieving an impressive accuracy rate of over 80%.\n\nMy role extended beyond technical aspects, as I strategically applied my computer science skills and business insights to conduct comprehensive market research, project sales, and assess risks and costs. The primary focus throughout was on enhancing the user experience, aligning with industry standards and user expectations. The experience went beyond project work, encompassing rigorous training in project management, design processes, and essential business skills.\n\nNotably, our efforts garnered recognition from a panel of professionals representing various industries. Their recommendation for further project development, accompanied by access to resources for potential funding, validated the impact and potential of our solution. This experience not only showcased my ability to contribute to innovative solutions but also highlighted my commitment to practical, results-driven collaboration in a professional setting.",
